    <section id="About" >
        <div class="container">
            <h2>About Us</h2>
            <div class="about-section">
                <div class="about-content">
                   <p> Our Inventory Management System (IMS) centralizes and automates inventory tracking and management 
                    at Dire Dawa University. With real-time updates, user access control, and automatic report generation,
                     it addresses resource mismanagement and inefficiencies. The user-friendly interface enhances operational 
                     efficiency, reduces waste, and ensures resources support academic and administrative activities. 
                     The IMS also boosts transparency and accountability in resource use, aiding the university's long-term goals. </p>
                     <p> We support six key roles: Admins handle employee registration and governance; Store Managers manage inventory,
                        logistics, and reporting; Store Keepers handle daily storage operations, inventory updates, and borrowing history; 
                        Department Heads lead academically, authorize employees, and manage borrowing; University Employees search items,
                         manage profiles, and track borrowing history; Maintenance Technicians ensure facilities are in top condition.</p>
             </div>
